  "id": "cumulative-frequency",
  "term": "cumulative frequency",
  "definition": "Cumulative frequency is the running total of frequencies across ordered classes or score ranges, found by adding each class frequency to all those that came before it. It shows how many observations have accumulated up to each point in the distribution.",
